# Supabase Data API — explicit GRANTs on public tables

This app uses the Supabase Data API (`supabase-js`, PostgREST). Every **new** `public` table must include explicit role grants in the **same migration** that creates it (after RLS is enabled and policies are defined).

**Deadline:** enforced on existing projects **2026-10-30** (new projects from **2026-05-30**). Missing grants cause PostgREST `42501` errors.

## Migration checklist

1. `CREATE TABLE public.<name> ...`
2. `ALTER TABLE public.<name> ENABLE ROW LEVEL SECURITY;`
3. `CREATE POLICY ...` (match app access: usually `authenticated` only; avoid `anon` unless intentional)
4. Explicit `GRANT`s for Data API roles

## Grant pattern

Default for tables behind RLS (no anonymous access):

```sql
grant select, insert, update, delete on public.your_table to authenticated;
grant select, insert, update, delete on public.your_table to service_role;
```

Only if the table is intentionally readable without login:

```sql
grant select on public.your_table to anon;
```

Tune privileges per table (e.g. read-only config: `grant select` only to `authenticated`).

## When editing migrations

- Do not add `CREATE TABLE public.*` without accompanying `GRANT`s in that file.
- When adding a new table to an existing feature, mirror grants used on similar tables in this repo.
- `service_role` bypasses RLS; use for scripts (`lib/supabase/service.ts`) only where appropriate.
